course: dictionary
lesson: 10641
title: Unicorn: a myth, a joke and a money word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so check the words around it to find the right one. «The unicorn galloped across the meadow, its single horn shining.» Galloped, meadow and horn are the clues, so unicorn means the magical animal from stories.
explain: Now read: «Her new company is a unicorn, worth over a billion dollars.» Company and billion are the clues. Here a unicorn is a money word for a new company that has grown very valuable. Swap in your meaning: does the sentence still make sense?
explain: Sometimes the word means something rare. «Honest referees are as rare as a unicorn.» The comparison tells you it means something rare and wonderful that is very hard to find. When the meaning is still unclear, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A unicorn is a noun: a unicorn, unicorns.
fact: A unicorn is a magical animal from stories and legends. It looks like a white horse with one long, straight, twisted horn on its forehead.
fact: Informal: «a unicorn» can mean something rare and wonderful that is very hard to find, as in «as rare as a unicorn».
fact: In money talk, a unicorn is a new company that has become worth over a billion dollars.
fact: Unicorns are not real. Long ago, traders sold narwhal tusks in Europe as «unicorn horns»; the tusk is really a long spiral tooth.
exercise: «The unicorn galloped across the meadow.» What is a unicorn in this sentence? | A type of flower | A king's servant | A horse that wins races | *A magical animal from stories
exercise: In money talk, what is a unicorn? | *A new company worth over a billion dollars | A very old castle | A bank that has closed | A coin from long ago
exercise: «Honest referees are as rare as a unicorn.» What does unicorn mean here? | *Something rare and wonderful that is very hard to find | A big rhino | A horse with a horn
exercise: Which animal was sold as a unicorn horn, but was really a long spiral tooth? | Seal | Dolphin | *Narwhal | Polar bear
test: Which animal is the national animal of Scotland? | Red deer | Golden eagle | Wolf | *Unicorn
test: Why do scientists say unicorns are a good example of a myth? | Because they have long tusks | Because they are very fast | *Because unicorns are not real | Because they live in Scotland
exam: A sentence reads: «Her new company is a unicorn, worth over a billion dollars.» What does unicorn mean? | A rare animal in the zoo | A shiny old coin | *A new company worth over a billion dollars | A magical horse with a golden horn
